  "label": "Dangerous Person Stereotype",
  "description": "This stereotype involves portraying individuals as inherently dangerous or unstable, often based on their behavior or appearance. It is used to justify fear, avoidance, or hostility toward the person, and can be used to stigmatize or marginalize them. This stereotype is often applied to people who are perceived as emotionally volatile, unpredictable, or prone to outbursts, which aligns with the visual metaphor of the man being engulfed in flames.",
